{%- comment -%}
  Real User Monitoring beacon.

  Included from layout/theme.liquid, immediately before </body>. Loads deferred
  and off the critical path — this measures page speed and must not cost any.

  Why we self-host and beacon to our own dashboard instead of sending a GA4
  event: GA4 runs through Shopify's Google channel web pixel, which is
  sandboxed, so window.gtag does not exist in theme scope. Re-adding gtag.js to
  the theme would re-introduce the duplicate-GA4 problem the 2026-07-24 tag
  audit fixed and add ~100KB to every page. Measurement Protocol would put the
  api_secret in client-side source. So: our own collector.

  The endpoint is a first-party subdomain on purpose. It was briefly on an
  ngrok-free.dev tunnel, which appears in ad-blocker filter lists and would have
  quietly biased the sample toward users who don't block. rum.realskincare.com
  is same-site, so it is not filtered, and it needs no CORS preflight.

  Set rum_sample below 1.0 to sample down if traffic grows.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign rum_endpoint = 'https://rum.realskincare.com/api/rum'
  assign rum_sample = 1.0
-%}

<script>
  window.__RSC_RUM = {
    endpoint: {{ rum_endpoint | json }},
    sample: {{ rum_sample }},
    template: {{ template.name | json }}
  };
</script>
<script src="{{ 'rsc-rum.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
